<title>SLOVENIA: Slovenia raises gasoline prices by 9.5 percent.</title>
<headline>Slovenia raises gasoline prices by 9.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Slovenian government said on Thursday it would raise gasoline prices by 9.5 percent on Friday due to higher taxes, trade margins and higher costs of crude oil.</p>
<p>The new price of a litre of unleaded gasoline will be 85.8 tolars ($0.56).</p>
<p>Last year, prices increased by a total 9.4 percent.</p>
<p>-- Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
</text>
